INSERT INTO ai_learning_lessons (
  id,
  learning_path_id,
  title,
  description,
  content_type,
  content,
  duration_minutes,
  order_index,
  learning_objectives
) VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  'f8a9b0c1-d2e3-4f5a-6b7c-8d9e0f1a2b3c',
  'Writing Your First Playwright Test',
  'Learn test structure, locators, actions, and assertions through hands-on examples',
  'article',
  $$# Writing Your First Playwright Test

## Test Anatomy

Every Playwright test has this structure:

```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('description of what you are testing', async ({ page }) => {
  // 1. Navigate
  await page.goto('https://example.com');

  // 2. Interact (click, type, etc.)
  await page.click('button');

  // 3. Assert (check results)
  await expect(page.locator('h1')).toBeVisible();
});
```

:::tip Test Structure
**AAA Pattern:**
- **Arrange** - Set up (navigate to page)
- **Act** - Do something (click, fill forms)
- **Assert** - Verify results (check what happened)
:::

## Your First Real Test

:::playwright-practice language=typescript | height=450px | title=Write Your First Test | testUrl=https://playwright.dev
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('homepage loads correctly', async ({ page }) => {
  // Arrange: Go to the website
  await page.goto('https://playwright.dev');

  // Act: Wait for page to load (automatic)

  // Assert: Check the title
  await expect(page).toHaveTitle(/Playwright/);

  // Assert: Check heading is visible
  const heading = page.locator('h1');
  await expect(heading).toBeVisible();

  console.log('✅ Test passed!');
});
:::

## Page Fixtures Deep Dive

The `{ page }` in your test is a **fixture** - Playwright automatically:
1. Creates a fresh browser context
2. Opens a new page
3. Gives it to your test
4. Closes everything after the test

**Benefits:**
- ✅ Each test is isolated (fresh start)
- ✅ No manual cleanup needed
- ✅ Tests can run in parallel

```typescript
test('fixture example', async ({ page }) => {
  // 'page' is ready to use immediately
  await page.goto('https://example.com');

  // After test finishes, page is automatically closed
});
```

## Locators: Finding Elements

**Locators** tell Playwright which element to interact with. Think of them as GPS coordinates for page elements.

### Locator Priority Order (Best to Worst)

1. **getByRole** (BEST - accessible, semantic)
2. **getByLabel** (Good for forms)
3. **getByPlaceholder** (Good for inputs)
4. **getByText** (Good for links/buttons)
5. **getByTestId** (Stable, requires setup)
6. **CSS/XPath** (LAST RESORT - fragile)

### 1. getByRole (Recommended!)

```typescript
// Buttons
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).click();

// Links
await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'About Us' }).click();

// Headings
await page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Welcome' });

// Text inputs
await page.getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Email' }).fill('test@example.com');

// Checkboxes
await page.getByRole('checkbox', { name: 'I agree' }).check();
```

:::success Why getByRole?
- ✅ Matches how screen readers work (accessibility)
- ✅ Resilient to UI changes
- ✅ Semantic and readable
:::

### 2. getByLabel (Forms)

```typescript
// Labels are connected to inputs
await page.getByLabel('Email address').fill('user@example.com');
await page.getByLabel('Password').fill('secret123');
await page.getByLabel('Remember me').check();
```

### 3. getByText

```typescript
// Click a button by its text
await page.getByText('Sign In').click();

// Find specific text
await expect(page.getByText('Welcome back!')).toBeVisible();
```

### 4. getByTestId (Stable IDs)

```typescript
// In your HTML: <button data-testid="submit-btn">Submit</button>
await page.getByTestId('submit-btn').click();

// Good for dynamic content
await expect(page.getByTestId('user-profile')).toContainText('John');
```

:::playwright-practice language=typescript | height=450px | title=Practice Locators | testUrl=https://playwright.dev
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('practice different locators', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('https://playwright.dev');

  // Try getByRole - most reliable!
  const getStartedLink = page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Get started' });
  await expect(getStartedLink).toBeVisible();

  // Try finding heading by role
  const heading = page.getByRole('heading', { level: 1 });
  await expect(heading).toBeVisible();

  console.log('✅ Locators working perfectly!');
});
:::

## Common Actions

### Navigation
```typescript
// Go to URL
await page.goto('https://example.com');

// Go back/forward
await page.goBack();
await page.goForward();

// Reload
await page.reload();
```

### Clicks
```typescript
// Simple click
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).click();

// Double click
await page.getByText('Select').dblclick();

// Right click
await page.getByText('Menu').click({ button: 'right' });
```

### Typing
```typescript
// Fill input (clears first, then types)
await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('test@example.com');

// Type (doesn't clear first)
await page.locator('input').type('hello');

// Press keyboard keys
await page.getByLabel('Search').press('Enter');
await page.keyboard.press('Tab');
```

### Checkboxes & Radio Buttons
```typescript
// Check
await page.getByLabel('I agree').check();

// Uncheck
await page.getByLabel('Newsletter').uncheck();

// Radio button
await page.getByLabel('Option A').check();
```

### Dropdowns
```typescript
// Select by label
await page.locator('select').selectOption('Option 1');

// Select by value
await page.locator('select').selectOption({ value: 'opt1' });
```

## Assertions (Checking Results)

```typescript
// Page assertions
await expect(page).toHaveTitle('My App');
await expect(page).toHaveURL('https://example.com/dashboard');

// Element visibility
await expect(page.getByText('Welcome')).toBeVisible();
await expect(page.getByText('Loading...')).toBeHidden();

// Text content
await expect(page.locator('h1')).toHaveText('Dashboard');
await expect(page.locator('.message')).toContainText('Success');

// Counts
await expect(page.locator('.item')).toHaveCount(5);

// Attributes
await expect(page.locator('input')).toHaveAttribute('type', 'email');

// States
await expect(page.getByLabel('Email')).toBeEnabled();
await expect(page.getByRole('button')).toBeDisabled();
```

:::warning Wait for It!
Playwright automatically waits for elements, but you can adjust:
```typescript
// Custom timeout
await expect(page.locator('.slow-element')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 });
```
:::

## Complete Example: Login Test

:::playwright-practice language=typescript | height=500px | title=Complete Example Test | testUrl=https://example.com
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('verify example.com page', async ({ page }) => {
  // Arrange: Navigate to page
  await page.goto('https://example.com');

  // Assert: Check page title
  await expect(page).toHaveTitle(/Example Domain/);

  // Assert: Find heading using getByRole
  const heading = page.getByRole('heading');
  await expect(heading).toBeVisible();
  await expect(heading).toContainText('Example');

  // Assert: Find paragraph text
  const paragraph = page.getByText('This domain is for use');
  await expect(paragraph).toBeVisible();

  // Assert: Find "More information" link
  const moreInfoLink = page.getByRole('link', { name: 'More information' });
  await expect(moreInfoLink).toBeVisible();

  console.log('✅ All assertions passed! Test complete.');
});
:::

## Test Organization Best Practices

### 1. Descriptive Test Names
```typescript
// ❌ Bad
test('test 1', async ({ page }) => {});

// ✅ Good
test('user can add item to cart', async ({ page }) => {});
test('displays error for invalid email', async ({ page }) => {});
```

### 2. Group Related Tests
```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe('Authentication', () => {
  test('user can log in', async ({ page }) => {
    // Login test
  });

  test('user can log out', async ({ page }) => {
    // Logout test
  });

  test('shows error for wrong password', async ({ page }) => {
    // Error test
  });
});
```

### 3. Use beforeEach for Setup
```typescript
test.describe('Dashboard Tests', () => {
  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    // This runs before EACH test
    await page.goto('https://example.com');
    await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('user@example.com');
    await page.getByLabel('Password').fill('password123');
    await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign In' }).click();
  });

  test('can view profile', async ({ page }) => {
    // Already logged in from beforeEach!
    await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Profile' }).click();
    await expect(page.locator('h1')).toHaveText('My Profile');
  });

  test('can update settings', async ({ page }) => {
    // Also already logged in!
    await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Settings' }).click();
  });
});
```

## Summary

**What you learned:**
- ✅ Test structure: import, test(), async/await, page fixture
- ✅ AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert
- ✅ Locator priority: getByRole → getByLabel → getByText → getByTestId
- ✅ Common actions: goto, click, fill, check
- ✅ Assertions: toBeVisible, toHaveText, toHaveURL
- ✅ Test organization: describe, beforeEach, clear names

**Next steps:**
- Practice writing tests for your own web apps
- Learn about advanced patterns (Page Objects, fixtures)
- Explore CI/CD integration for automated testing
$$,
  40,
  2,
  ARRAY[
    'Write well-structured Playwright tests',
    'Use semantic locators effectively',
    'Perform common browser actions',
    'Create assertions to verify behavior',
    'Organize tests with describe and beforeEach'
  ]
);

